1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,727
Every student job hunting
asks the same two things.

2
00:00:03,977 --> 00:00:06,520
What am I missing, and what proves it.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,587
This is SkillProof running.

4
00:00:08,837 --> 00:00:12,248
It reads her resume,
looks through her public

5
00:00:12,248 --> 00:00:15,659
repositories, and records
which file proved which skill.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,963
Forty seven percent ready
for ML Engineer roles.

7
00:00:19,213 --> 00:00:23,868
Each block is a skill, and wider
means more employers ask for it.

8
00:00:24,118 --> 00:00:28,378
She could reach eighty nine just
by proving what she already shows.

9
00:00:28,628 --> 00:00:31,905
Her gap is unproven, not unknown.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,576
Every skill the role asks for,
grouped by how well she proves it.

11
00:00:37,826 --> 00:00:40,036
Open one for the exact file.

12
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,829
SQL is on her resume, it
appears in sixty four percent

13
00:00:46,829 --> 00:00:50,658
of listings, and it is in
none of her ten repositories.

14
00:00:50,908 --> 00:00:53,758
So the product tests things
instead of believing them.

15
00:00:54,008 --> 00:00:58,031
Four questions that adapt:
one right, the next is harder.

16
00:00:58,281 --> 00:01:00,705
Python comes back at a hundred percent.

17
00:01:00,955 --> 00:01:05,002
That makes it tested, and the score
moves to forty nine point five.

18
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,034
Now the same four questions
for SQL, the skill

19
00:01:12,034 --> 00:01:14,730
she claimed but we
could not find anywhere.

20
00:01:14,980 --> 00:01:16,657
Twenty one percent.

21
00:01:16,907 --> 00:01:20,178
The label still reads on
your resume, not tested,

22
00:01:20,178 --> 00:01:23,085
and the score edges down instead of up.

23
00:01:23,335 --> 00:01:27,788
Claiming a skill is not proving it, and
this is the product saying so out loud.

24
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,317
The plan is built from what is left.

25
00:01:35,567 --> 00:01:40,444
Eight weeks at eight hours, nothing
over budget, prerequisites first.

26
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:45,557
Every task says why it is there
and ends in something she can show.

27
00:01:45,807 --> 00:01:47,810
Nothing is fixed until approval.

28
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,428
Four ways to record what she actually did.

29
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,103
She marks the first task done.

30
00:01:56,353 --> 00:01:57,947
The score does not move.

31
00:01:58,197 --> 00:02:00,727
Marking a task done is a claim.

32
00:02:00,977 --> 00:02:02,974
Proof is code, or a test.

33
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,743
So she links the repository
she actually built.

34
00:02:06,993 --> 00:02:12,852
The agent scans it, finds a Dockerfile,
a FastAPI service and a GitHub Actions

35
00:02:12,852 --> 00:02:18,293
workflow, and the score jumps from
forty nine to fifty seven point six.

36
00:02:18,543 --> 00:02:23,008
The box underneath names exactly
which weeks moved and what was

37
00:02:23,008 --> 00:02:27,473
added, and anything she edited
herself stays as she left it.

38
00:02:27,723 --> 00:02:30,786
She then tests Docker and retakes SQL.

39
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,210
Sixty three percent ready.

40
00:02:35,460 --> 00:02:38,607
Three skills now carry
the tested seal, and the

41
00:02:38,607 --> 00:02:41,404
sentence under the score
has changed with them.

42
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,798
Flat while she was claiming.

43
00:02:44,048 --> 00:02:46,130
Rising every time she proved something.

44
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:47,228
SkillProof.

45
00:02:47,478 --> 00:02:49,368
Skills proven, not claimed.
